        "text": "|\n| | |\n# 2026 Elections\n#### July 2026\nMy Campaign Website.\n# 2019 Special Elections\n#### March, 2019\n2019 Special Election page.\n# 2018 Elections\n#### November, 2018\nElection coverage for the November 2018 is here.\n# 2016 Election Coverage\n#### August, 2016\nElection coverage for the November 2016 General Election is here.\n# Changing Times\n#### July, 2016\nAfter appointing Phil Hu to fill Mayor Trish Spencer's unexpired term and making interim Superintendent Sean McPhetridge the permanent Superintendent, AUSD was able to reach one year agreements with its labor unions.\nWith all of this good news it would appear AUSD can look forward to smooth sailing. The Board selected Gray Harris from a pool of 5 applicants for Niel Tam. The Board placed a ballot measure to renew the parcel tax, expiring in 2018.\n# Facilities Master Plan Implementation Process\n#### November 19, 2014\nIn 2015, the school board will have to decide how to prioritize how to spend over $65 million for elementary and middle school sites. The initial plans approved by the former school board will have to reviewed to determine what timeline is feasible and the impact on school operations.\n# New CAASPP Test Results Released\n#### September 13, 2015\nIn 2013, California began transitioning over the Common Core curriculum. The first achievement results from Common Core were released in September, 2015. Here are achievement and demographic data for Alameda Unified. Alameda charter schools achievement and demographic is also available.\n## School Locator with 2002-2010 API Data links\nView Larger\n## School Board Meeting Recaps\nLooking for a specific agenda item from a school board meeting? Start here: Monthly Recaps. Cannot find the item by reviewing the agendas from the monthly recap? Google lets you search mikemcmahon.info by using a specific syntax. In the Google search box, put www.mikemcmahon.info followed by a colon and the specific term you are looking for. For example, if you wanted to find information about homework on my website only you would type www.mikemcmahon.info:homework\nCA News Stories Related to Education\nAUSD Board Policies and Administrative Regulations Enter: ALAMEDA for username and public for the password\nAdditional Materials on the Website\n- Alameda Point Development Section\n- Labor Settlements with Employee Groups\n- Equity/Excellence Section\n- Cycle of Inquiry Section\n- Point of Views on Public Education Section\n| |\n|\nTOP\n##### Comments. Questions. Broken links? Bad spelling! Incorrect Grammar? Let me know at webmaster.\nLast modified: February, 2014 material the use of which has not always been specifically authorized by the copyright owner. I am making such material available in my effort to advance understanding of education issues vital to a democracy. I believe this constitutes a 'fair use' of any such copyrighted material as provided for in section 107 of the US Copyright Law. In accordance with Title 17 U.S.C. Section 107, the material on this site is distributed without profit to those who have expressed a prior interest in receiving the included information for research and educational purposes. If you wish to use copyrighted material from this site for purposes of your own that go beyond 'fair use', you must obtain permission from the copyright owner.",
